{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfdtJm5JQLmbBAr6TxHwx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I submitted an equal-weight portfolio of 188 slow trend-following signals: the 63-, 126- and 252-day time-series momentum signals plus the 50/200-day moving-average signal, for all 47 industries. Its training Sharpe is only 0.22 and it **FAILED** the validation test, which was the only backtest I ran.\n\nI stopped at one backtest on purpose. The research ends at the first PASS, so retrying until one passes would mean picking the portfolio based on the validation data. That PASS would then be a false positive and wouldn't tell you anything about future returns. Running many backtests against a single pass/fail bar works the same way: something eventually passes by chance.\n\nThe training data also suggests there isn't much to find at the level of individual signals. Their Sharpe ratios in 1970–84 have a slightly negative correlation (−0.10) with their Sharpe ratios in 1985–99. Ranking and picking individual signals would mostly fit noise. The only effect that showed up as a group was slow trend-following, and even that was positive in two of the three decades but lost money in the middle one. This is a modest, diversified bet, not a strong signal, and your significance bar did not confirm it on 2000–2012."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":386,"cache_read_input_tokens":9749,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":386},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c62b9df1-5a7b-4714-9246-5cdc2a9a8fdc","uuid":"b86f1aa1-4951-4fcd-ba91-502fe5cbfa92","timestamp":"2026-10-02T18:29:43.682Z","request_id":"req_011CfdtJkmByWgdc6Bin3cyC"}
